From c25e112112dbfc07d8d11f5b136a0b3f4ffed7d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:38:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03981/11362] [outer-loop] ARC induction: goal-repair loop for
 degenerate is_level_complete + default-ON truncation fix

Two operator-greenlit changes (2026-06-25):

1. GOAL-REPAIR LOOP (arc_llm_reinduction.execute_bounded_llm_reinduction): when the LLM-induced
   is_level_complete is degenerate (constant `return False` / unreachable exact-match) and fails
   _goal_satisfiability_check, substitute the exemplar-derived _nonzero_count_predicate fallback and
   re-check satisfiability against the SAME engine; if reachable, plan toward it instead of burning
   the round on an engine-refactor (which never targets the goal). Only fires when a
   previous_level_complete_grid exemplar is present AND the fallback is reachable -> backward-
   compatible (existing tests, which pass no exemplar, are unaffected). Downstream plan-reaches-goal
   + reproduction gate still decide a real level-up, so a loose proxy cannot fabricate a solve -- it
   only unblocks the search. New _repair_degenerate_goal helper + 5 tests (incl. a no-exemplar
   control proving the repair is the cause). Addresses the dominant lp85 L2 failure the truncation
   fix alone did NOT solve.

2. TRUNCATION FIX DEFAULT-ON (arc_executable_world_model.generate): CARNOT_ARC_CODEONLY_INDUCE now
   defaults ON (opt out =0). Strict improvement: valid code in ~10s where the unpatched induce path
   truncated to 0 code at 450s. Verified live with the env unset (10.5s, valid engine+is_level_complete).
   Induce-scoped; gap-filler/refactor callers untouched.

Tests: 5 new goal-repair + 11 existing reinduction pass; ruff + arc-orphan-solver-lint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
